    "title": "Johnston man charged with DUI after crash involving motorcycle - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Sarah Bawden ,\n2 days ago\nJOHNSTON, R.I. (WPRI) — A Johnston man was charged with driving under the influence after a crash that injured a motorcyclist over the weekend, according to police.\nOfficers were called to Central Avenue Sunday evening after receiving reports of a crash involving a motorcycle.\nPolice said the motorcyclist, who has not been identified, was brought to Rhode Island Hospital to be treated for unspecified injuries.\nThe driver who hit the motorcyclist, identified by police as a 41-year-old man, was taken into custody.\nPolice said he's been charged with driving under the influence and refusing to submit a chemical test.\nDownload the WPRI 12 and Pinpoint Weather 12 apps to get breaking news and weather alerts.\nWatch 12 News Now on WPRI.com or with the free WPRI 12+ TV app .\nFollow us on social media:\n[sailthru_widget name=\"Sailthru Widget Block\" sailthru_list=\"Daily News\" title=\"Daily Roundup\"] Copyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed.\nFor the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WPRI.com.",
    "summary": "Officers were called to Central Avenue Sunday evening after receiving reports of a crash involving a motorcycle. Police said the motorcyclist, who has not been identified, was brought to Rhode Island Hospital to be treated for unspecified injuries. The driver who hit the motorcyclist, identified by police as a 41-year-old man, was taken into custody. Police said he's been charged with driving under the influence and refusing to submit a chemical test. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WPRI.com.",
